JUCE patch: let the app add items to a hosted VST3 plugin's parameter context menu.

Why: a VST3 plugin asks the host for a context menu on a parameter with
IComponentHandler3::createContextMenu(view, &paramId). Stock JUCE ignores the ParamID and returns
a menu holding only the plugin's own items. This patch remembers the ParamID and, when the menu
is shown, appends the items an app-supplied callback adds (juce::VST3PluginFormat::
setHostContextMenuExtension). The callback's items carry their own PopupMenu::Item action, which
JUCE already runs on the message thread after the menu closes (also in the async menu path used
when JUCE_MODAL_LOOPS_PERMITTED is off). Nothing changes for an instance with no callback.

Applied by cmake/ApplyJucePatch.cmake (FetchContent PATCH_COMMAND); mechanism and how to update
it for a new JUCE tag: docs/development/juce-patches.md. The JUCE files use CRLF line endings.

